A||||3||pHoOl||Installing Fog lights||||1||
Z||000000||pHoOl||10-31-2000||10:44 PM||||Well, i finally splurged and bought the 30 dollar annoying yellow lights.  I've heard that they increase visiblity quite well, plus i'm worried about my white GT not being able to be seen in snow.  Anyway, enough with the small talk.....<P>I'm still trying to find out where exactly to bolt them on.  I know that i don't want to drill holes in the front fascia to mount them in the mouth.  I saw some nice metal parts hanging down in there, and figured these would make good candidates.  Am i right?<P>I've decided to put the switch in where the ash tray is, and i'm trying to figure out the best way to run the wires through the firewall.  I've heard that there are holes down by the gas pedal, but haven't seen it.  thought also of running it through where the steering rod goes, but didn't see where the other side of that hole was with the hood up.  <P>Any thoughts on how to get it though cleanly?  I'm trying to make it look as professional as possible.<P>Thanks for all help<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/pHoOl_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||kinboyatuwo||11-01-2000||12:06 PM||||Okay there is one easy to find whole in the firewall.  Behind the gas pedal and up to the left.  Another easy way to find it is to go into the front compartment, more toward the center than the brakefluid resivoir but close, down an inch or two.  There might be a rubber or plastic cap over it, but it is there.  <BR>The fog lights i have seen mounted flush in the facia or in the mouth.  The mouth mount looks pretty secure, there is some metal to use just feel and look around, would be easy if you take the fromt end off.  I have pulled mine off and it is not too hard with another person to help.<P>Good luck by the way<BR>kinboyatuwo||||reg||10
Z||000002||SibERThuG||11-01-2000||12:17 PM||||I drilled right into the fascia. I went through that firewall near the gas pedal (it is there) and I ran the wire through the center console (I also put a switch in my ashtray) and through the rear firewall and to the battery. My ground is hooked up-up front so that there wasn't a lot of wiring to do. It's hard and it sux to do, but they do increase visibility quite well. It was worth it.<P>------------------<BR>Robbie<BR>88' Formula||||reg||10
Z||000003||Oreif||11-01-2000||02:36 PM||||I made a bracket that mounted behind the front fascia and the lights sit just inside the rear of the "mouth".<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/DSC00007_1.jpg"> <BR>||||reg||1
